I fixed both: yoyo watch lint with no lint command detected, and bare yoyo docs, now exit 2 instead of 0. Committed as 000335df, titled Part of #982: …. Build, all tests, clippy with -D warnings and the fmt check all pass.

What changed
• `src/watch.rs`: the "no lint command detected" branch now returns the same usage exit code (2) that bare watch got in 2b5a5c17. The shell watch command already passes that code on as the exit status. The REPL /watch lint ignores it, prints the same text and doesn't exit.
• `src/commands_project.rs`: both "no crate given" paths (/docs, and /docs followed only by spaces) now return a new usage code, also 2. docs <crate> behaves as before: 0 if found, 1 if not found or docs.rs can't be reached.
• `src/dispatch_sub.rs`: one test changed. test_try_dispatch_subcommand_docs used to run bare docs inside the test process, which would now exit the test binary. It now checks the input the docs command builds plus the status it returns, so it no longer covers the docs dispatch path itself.
• `docs/src/usage/commands.md`: the exit-code paragraphs now describe both changes. That makes 4 files instead of the 3 the task allowed: the docs code lives in commands_project.rs, and the docs page needed fixing too.

Tests
• The existing watch test now checks watch lint both ways: 2 in an empty folder (and nothing gets installed), 0 in a folder with a Cargo.toml.
• A new test checks that all the docs-without-a-crate forms exit 2.
• I removed the new return as a check, and the test failed at the watch lint line; with it restored the test passes.

Run on the built binary, from an empty folder with stdin from `/dev/null`
```
yoyo watch lint  -> 2
yoyo docs        -> 2
yoyo watch status -> 0   (unchanged)
```

